  "notes": "Relay 1-CLS-RLY-3/4-18 is 'de-energize to function' logic; failure of coil (still receiving 135 VDC) caused relay to de-energize as if a real HI CLS condition existed, despite actual containment pressure being normal (~10 psia). No SSCs were inoperable/contributed per licensee; ESF systems all functioned as designed. Similar-event relay (Robinson Unit 2, 2015, IRIS 320473) was a random failure not in single-point-vulnerability configuration, so did not cause a trip there; modeled as stub LER per instructions despite non-standard reference format (IRIS number used instead of LER number, so key set from available identifying info '1-2015' as best approximation of report year; true LER number not stated in narrative)."
